! Taking over a wiki file

If a wiki so far exists only as a single `index.html` on a computer or a USB stick, you can take it over into MWS that way. No tiddler is copied by hand.

* Open the ''admin page'' and click ''Take over a wiki file'' in the ''Create a wiki'' dropdown.
* Choose the saved `index.html` of the wiki. It must have been saved with ''TiddlyWiki 5''.
* Choose the target: a ''new wiki'' (with a name and a slug) or an ''existing wiki''.
* Click ''Check the file''. The server reads the file and shows what would happen: new, changed, unchanged and deleted tiddlers, the system tiddlers it contains and the plugins that are left out. Nothing is written yet.
* If you want the layout, tag and theme settings of the old wiki ($:/ tiddlers), tick ''Also import system tiddlers''.
* Only ''Import now'' writes. For an existing wiki you choose beforehand whether to ''Replace'' (the wiki becomes the file, a snapshot is taken first) or to ''Merge'' (only new and changed tiddlers are written, nothing is deleted).

!! Rights

* ''Merge'' needs the same right as saving a tiddler.
* ''Replace'' deletes tiddlers and therefore needs administrator rights on the bag of the wiki.
* Clicking the restore button on a snapshot brings the old state back. That, too, is undoable, because a snapshot is taken first again.

!! What is not taken over

* Plugins, themes, libraries and language packs: a wiki gets those from its recipe ([[Bags und Rollen]]).
* TiddlyWiki 2 files, password-protected files and files without tiddlers are refused with a clear message.
* Very large files: the server limit is 50 MB (changeable via `MWS_WIKI_FILE_SIZE_LIMIT`).